NAME
       lvremove - delete logical volumes

SYNOPSIS
       lvremove [-f] [-y] LV|VG...

DESCRIPTION
       lvremove deletes a logical volume and gives its space back to the
       volume group. Everything stored on it is lost. Given a VG name instead
       of an LV, it removes every LV in that VG.

       An LV whose file system is mounted (or a swap LV in use) cannot be
       removed: unmount it (or swapoff) first, and remove its line from
       /etc/fstab, or the next boot will fail waiting for it.

       For an active LV, lvremove asks before it deletes.

OPTIONS
       -f, --force
              Do not ask for confirmation.

       -y, --yes
              Answer yes to the question.

EXAMPLES
       Retire the LV old in VG vgdata:

           umount /old
           vi /etc/fstab        (delete the /old line)
           lvremove -y /dev/vgdata/old

SEE ALSO
       lvcreate(8), vgremove(8), umount(8), lvm(8)
